│ The core issue seems to be that the subst_vars_replace function is │
│ modifying the source list in place, but not returning the modified │
│ string. This means the updated source[0] isn't being properly used │
│ by Sphinx during the HTML generation process. By adding return     │
│ result to the end of the function, we ensure that the modified     │
