│ The core issue is that the source-read event isn’t correctly       │
│ modifying the included files. The subst_vars_replace function is   │
│ called, it does replace the &REPLACE_ME; string within the         │
│ included file, but the modified content isn’t propagated to the    │
│ final HTML output. This likely stems from how Sphinx handles the   │
│ source variable passed to the event handler. The source variable   │
│ appears to be a string containing the entire file content, not a   │
│ list of strings suitable for modification.  The replace method is  │
│ operating on this single string, not on a list of strings.         │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix is to modify the subst_vars_replace function to split the  │
│ source string into a list of lines before performing the           │
│ replacement, and then join the lines back together after the       │
│ replacement. This ensures that each line is treated individually,  │
│ allowing the replacement to be applied correctly.                  │
│                                                                    │
